ompleteness | All target-required fields must be populated (directly or derived) | Reject/hold |\n| O4 – Row-length/structural | Row must have the expected column count/type | Reject |\n\n## 4. Error handling & disposition\n- **Reject** — unrecoverable parse/key failures (D1, D2, D4, N1, C1, C2, O1, O4).\n- **Hold** — required data missing but potentially sourceable (D7 missing `invoice_date`, O2 unresolvable vendor, N6 missing VAT basis).\n- **Flag/Review** — postable but needs a human decision (D3, D5, N2, N4, N6, C4, C5).\n- Each rejected/held/flagged row carries a **reason code** (D#/N#/C#/O#) and is written to a **quarantine log** — no silent drops.\n\n## 5. Controls & audit\n- **Control totals:** count of input rows = posted + rejected + held + flagged; sum of input `gross_amount` = sum of posted `gross_amount` (+quarantine totals).\n- **Reconciliation report:** `Σ net + Σ vat = Σ gross` within tolerance across the batch.\n- **Provenance:** record source file name, hash, row count, transformation version/timestamp; input file left **untouched**.\n- **Segregation:** sensitive identifiers masked; access restricted.\n\n## 6. Open items to confirm against the real file/target schema\n1. Actual source column names → finalize mapping classes (direct/rename/convert/derived).\n2. Exact target schema required columns.\n3. Approved currency allow-list and FX source.\n4. Zero-VAT/tax-code mapping and rounding policy.\n5. Whether `net_amount` is supplied or must be derived.\n\n---\n\n**Note:** this is a specification only — no code was written or run, and no files were read or modified. If you'd like, I can next turn this into concrete transformation + validation logic **and execute it** once you (a) re-upload the file or give its URI, and (b) confirm the target schema columns."